  // React usually handles this if we render null -> render component.
  // To support the "enter" transition from a mounted state, we use an animation keyframe or a mount-effect class.
  // Here we'll stick to the conditional class which works well if the component was unmounted.
  // However, since we keep it mounted during 'isClosing', we can use the state.

  // To ensure entrance animation works when switching projects (which doesn't unmount),
  // we might rely on the key prop or just the transition.

